// Libyan Arabic (ayl — Tripolitanian) — an Arabic VARIETY. Evaluated through phonemizeArabic(text, "libyan"): the
// MSA neural diacritizer restores short vowels, the MSA g2p runs, then the Libyan shifts (ق→ɡ, ج→ʒ, خ→χ;
// interdentals ث/ذ/ظ KEPT; ay→eː, aw→oː) transform it. Referee: wikipron ayl_arab_broad (HUMAN, fully-voweled
// DIALECTAL IPA, INDEPENDENT). Same pausal + gemination folds as MSA. The short-vowel restructuring gap (MSA
// diacritizer restores MSA vowels) is the documented tail, as for arz/apc — consonants only.
{
    "referees": [
        {
            "file": "ayl.wikipron-ayl-broad.tsv",
            "source": "wikipron ayl_arab broad (human)",
            "role": "primary"
        }
    ],
    "secondaryGap": "No independent secondary for Libyan Arabic: wikipron ayl broad is the only free dialectal-IPA source (no kaikki ayl, no epitran). The consonant fingerprint (ق→ɡ, ج→ʒ, خ→χ, kept interdentals) is corroborated against published Libyan phonology; the shared MSA vowels are the data-limited tail (as arz/apc).",
    "segmentJoin": true,
    // ⚠ NO PAUSAL FOLD. ar.jsonc strips a word-final short vowel because MSA's iʕrab case ending is not
    // pronounced in pause. THE SPOKEN DIALECTS DROPPED IʕRAB — a final short vowel here is lexical, not a case
    // ending, so stripping it scored its absence as free (the axis-deletion failure) AND fired asymmetrically,
    // since it ran as a preFold, before the symbol folds. Removing it moved this family +0.5 to +6.1pp.
    // Measured 2026-08-20; see docs/investigations/arz_referee_investigation.md.
    "folds": [
        {
            "pattern": "(.)\\1+",
            "replace": "$1",
            "note": "gemination (shadda): collapse doubling — length already stripped by the backbone"
        }
    ]
}
